                    "**2. Laws of Exponents:** Same as integers, but now with real bases and rational powers.",
                    "**3. Patterns:** $a^p \\cdot a^q = a^{p+q}$, $(a^p)^q = a^{pq}$."
                ],
                "algorithms": [
                    {
                        "steps": [
                            "**Rationalize $1/(\\sqrt{7}-2)$:**",
                            "Identify conjugate: $\\sqrt{7}+2$.",
                            "Multiply Top/Bottom: $(\\sqrt{7}+2) / ((\\sqrt{7}-2)(\\sqrt{7}+2))$.",
                            "Use $(a-b)(a+b) = a^2-b^2$: $(\\sqrt{7}+2) / (7 - 4)$.",
                            "Final result: $(\\sqrt{7}+2) / 3$."
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "boxes": [
                    {
                        "type": "info",
                        "html": "$a^0 = 1$ and $a^{1/n} = \\sqrt[n]{a}$."
                    }
